<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <meta name="description" content="Privacy Policy for the CSPC Suggestion and Feedback System — how we collect, use, and protect your information." />
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/responsive.css" />
  <style>
    /* ── Privacy Policy page styles ────────────────────────────── */
    .privacy-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a 0%, #1e3a5f 60%, #1a56db 100%);
      padding-block: var(--space-12) var(--space-10);
      text-align: center;
    }
    .privacy-hero__eyebrow {
      display: inline-block;
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }
    .privacy-hero__title {
      font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
      font-weight: 700;
      color: #fff;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }
    .privacy-hero__meta {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: rgba(255,255,255,0.55);
    }

    /* Content wrapper */
    .privacy-body {
      max-width: 820px;
      margin-inline: auto;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-6);
    }

    /* Academic notice banner */
    .notice-banner {
      background: var(--color-primary-light);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-primary);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    .notice-banner__icon {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
      flex-shrink: 0;
      line-height: 1;
      margin-top: 2px;
    }
    .notice-banner__text {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--color-primary-dark);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .notice-banner__text strong { font-weight: 600; }

    /* Table of contents */
    .toc {
      background: var(--color-bg-alt);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    }
    .toc__title {
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.07em;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
    }
    .toc__list {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--space-1);
      list-style: decimal;
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .toc__list a {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      color: var(--color-primary);
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: color var(--transition);
    }
    .toc__list a:hover { color: var(--color-primary-dark); text-decoration: underline; }

    /* Policy sections */
    .policy-section {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    }
    .policy-section__anchor {
      display: block;
      position: relative;
      top: -80px;
      visibility: hidden;
    }
    .policy-section__heading {
      font-size: 1.2rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--color-text);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      padding-bottom: var(--space-3);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-primary-light);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-3);
    }
    .policy-section__heading-num {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      width: 28px; height: 28px;
      background: var(--color-primary);
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      border-radius: 50%;
      flex-shrink: 0;
    }
    .policy-section p {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }
    .policy-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .policy-section ul,
    .policy-section ol {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }
    .policy-section ul { list-style: disc; }
    .policy-section ol { list-style: decimal; }
    .policy-section li {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      line-height: 1.75;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
    }
    .policy-section strong { color: var(--color-text); font-weight: 600; }
    .policy-section h3 {
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      margin-top: var(--space-4);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    /* Comparison table */
    .data-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }
    .data-table th {
      background: var(--color-bg-alt);
      color: var(--color-text);
      font-weight: 600;
      padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
      text-align: left;
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    }
    .data-table td {
      padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      vertical-align: top;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    .data-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: var(--color-bg-alt); }

    /* Inline tags */
    .tag {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: 2px 8px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      font-size: 0.75rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .tag--yes  { background: #d1fae5; color: #065f46; }
    .tag--no   { background: #fee2e2; color: #991b1b; }

    /* Contact card */
    .contact-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-5);
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
    .contact-card__icon { font-size: 2rem; flex-shrink: 0; line-height: 1; }
    .contact-card__content p {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }
    .contact-card__content p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    /* Back link */
    .back-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--color-text-muted);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
      transition: color var(--transition);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .back-link:hover { color: var(--color-primary); }

    /* Responsive overrides */
    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .privacy-body { padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4); }
      .contact-card { flex-direction: column; }
      .data-table, .data-table tbody, .data-table tr { display: block; }
      .data-table thead { display: none; }
      .data-table td {
        display: block;
        border-bottom: none;
        padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      }
      .data-table td::before {
        content: attr(data-label);
        font-weight: 600;
        color: var(--color-text);
        display: block;
        font-size: 0.75rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
        margin-bottom: 2px;
      }
      .data-table tr {
        border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
        border-radius: var(--radius);
        margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
        overflow: hidden;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <%- include('partials/navbar') %>

  <!-- Hero banner -->
  <section class="privacy-hero" aria-labelledby="privacyHeading">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="privacy-hero__eyebrow">CSPC Suggestion &amp; Feedback System</span>
      <h1 class="privacy-hero__title" id="privacyHeading">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="privacy-hero__meta">Last updated: September 2026 &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Academic / Project System</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main content -->
  <div class="privacy-body">

    <a href="/" class="back-link" id="privacyBackLink">&#8592; Back to Home</a>

    <!-- Academic notice -->
    <div class="notice-banner" role="note" aria-label="Academic project notice">
      <span class="notice-banner__icon" aria-hidden="true">🎓</span>
      <div class="notice-banner__text">
        <strong>Academic / Project System.</strong> This system was developed as an academic project for
        Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC). It is not a commercial service. This policy describes
        the data the system actually collects and how it is used to operate the feedback platform.
        If you have questions, please use the contact information at the bottom of this page.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Table of contents -->
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Privacy policy sections">
      <p class="toc__title">Contents</p>
      <ol class="toc__list">
        <li><a href="#section-overview">Overview</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-who">Who This Policy Applies To</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-account-data">Account &amp; Authentication Data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-feedback-data">Feedback &amp; Submission Data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-anonymous">Anonymous vs. Identified Feedback</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-session">Session &amp; Technical Data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-use">How We Use Your Information</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-access">Who Can Access Your Data</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-storage">Database Storage</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-email">Email Communication</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-retention">Data Retention</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-security">Security Measures</a></li>
        <li><a href="#section-contact">Contact &amp; Questions</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <!-- 1. Overview -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-overview" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
        Overview
      </h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>CSPC Suggestion &amp; Feedback System</strong> is a web application that allows
        students and members of the Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges community to submit feedback,
        suggestions, complaints, concerns, and appreciation to authorized college administrators.
      </p>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains what personal information the system collects, how it is used
        to operate the feedback platform, and who can access it. We only collect information that is
        necessary to run the system. We do not sell or share your data with third parties outside of
        what is described below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Who -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-who" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
        Who This Policy Applies To
      </h2>
      <p>
        This policy applies to all users of the CSPC Suggestion &amp; Feedback System, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Registered students</strong> &mdash; users who create an account (via Google OAuth or email/password) and submit feedback.</li>
        <li><strong>Anonymous submissions</strong> &mdash; authenticated users who choose to submit a specific feedback item marked as anonymous.</li>
        <li><strong>Administrators</strong> &mdash; authorized CSPC personnel who review and respond to submitted feedback.</li>
        <li><strong>Visitors</strong> &mdash; anyone who browses public pages (such as this page) without logging in.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. Account data -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-account-data" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
        Account &amp; Authentication Data
      </h2>
      <p>The system supports two ways to create an account:</p>

      <h3>a) Google OAuth (&ldquo;Sign in with Google&rdquo;)</h3>
      <p>
        When you sign in using Google, the system receives the following information directly from
        Google&rsquo;s OAuth 2.0 service and stores it in the database:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Full name</strong> &mdash; from your Google profile (<code>displayName</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> &mdash; the primary email associated with your Google account.</li>
        <li><strong>Google account identifier (Google ID / <code>sub</code>)</strong> &mdash; a unique numeric
            identifier that Google assigns to your account, stored to link your Google account to your
            system account on future logins.</li>
        <li><strong>Profile picture URL (avatar)</strong> &mdash; the URL of your Google profile photo,
            if Google provides one. This URL is stored in the database. The current interface does not
            display it in profile views; only the first letter of your name is shown as an avatar in
            the navigation bar.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No Google access tokens or refresh tokens are stored by this system. Once you are authenticated,
        only your internal user ID, name, and role are kept in the server-side session.
      </p>

      <h3>b) Email &amp; Password Registration</h3>
      <p>
        If you register manually with an email address and password, the system stores:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Full name</strong> &mdash; as entered during registration.</li>
        <li><strong>Email address</strong> &mdash; stored in lowercase.</li>
        <li><strong>Password hash</strong> &mdash; your password is <em>never</em> stored in plain text.
            It is stored as a one-way bcrypt hash; the original password cannot be recovered from it.</li>
        <li><strong>Student ID</strong> (optional) &mdash; if provided during registration.</li>
        <li><strong>Department</strong> (optional) &mdash; if provided during registration.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Manual email/password accounts do not have a profile picture stored.</p>

      <h3>c) Account status and role</h3>
      <p>
        All accounts have a <strong>role</strong> (<code>student</code> or <code>admin</code>) and an
        <strong>active/inactive status</strong> managed in the database. Roles and active status are
        set server-side and cannot be changed by users through the interface.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Feedback data -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-feedback-data" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
        Feedback &amp; Submission Data
      </h2>
      <p>When you submit feedback, the system stores the following in the database:</p>
      <table class="data-table" aria-label="Feedback data fields stored by the system">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Description</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Reference number</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">A unique tracking identifier in the format <code>FB-YYYY-#####</code>, generated automatically.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Category</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">The category you selected (e.g., Academic, Facilities, Student Services).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Type</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">Suggestion, Complaint, Concern, General Feedback, or Appreciation.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Priority</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">Low, Medium, or High &mdash; selected when submitting.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Subject</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">The title/subject of your feedback item.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Description</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">The full text of your feedback or suggestion.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Anonymous flag</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">Whether you chose to submit anonymously (see Section 5).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Status</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">Current status: Submitted, Under Review, In Progress, Resolved, or Closed.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>User ID (submitter link)</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">A database foreign key linking the feedback to your account. Stored as <code>NULL</code> when you submit anonymously.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Field"><strong>Timestamps</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Description">Date and time the feedback was created and last updated.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        A <strong>status history log</strong> is maintained for each feedback item, recording every
        status change, the administrator who made it, and any note left by the administrator.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Administrator responses</strong> to your feedback are stored separately and are visible
        to you on the feedback detail page when you are logged in.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. Anonymous vs identified -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-anonymous" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
        Anonymous vs. Identified Feedback
      </h2>
      <p>
        You must be logged in to submit feedback. However, the submission form provides a
        <strong>&ldquo;Submit anonymously&rdquo;</strong> checkbox. Here is exactly how each mode works:
      </p>
      <table class="data-table" aria-label="Comparison of anonymous and identified feedback">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Aspect</th>
            <th>Identified Feedback</th>
            <th>Anonymous Feedback</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Aspect"><strong>Login required?</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Identified Feedback"><span class="tag tag--yes">Yes</span></td>
            <td data-label="Anonymous Feedback"><span class="tag tag--yes">Yes</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Aspect"><strong>User ID stored with feedback?</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Identified Feedback"><span class="tag tag--yes">Yes</span></td>
            <td data-label="Anonymous Feedback"><span class="tag tag--no">No &mdash; stored as NULL</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Aspect"><strong>Admins can see your name?</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Identified Feedback"><span class="tag tag--yes">Yes</span></td>
            <td data-label="Anonymous Feedback"><span class="tag tag--no">No</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Aspect"><strong>Visible on your own dashboard?</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Identified Feedback"><span class="tag tag--yes">Yes</span></td>
            <td data-label="Anonymous Feedback"><span class="tag tag--no">No &mdash; not linked to your account</span></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Aspect"><strong>Feedback content stored?</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Identified Feedback"><span class="tag tag--yes">Yes</span></td>
            <td data-label="Anonymous Feedback"><span class="tag tag--yes">Yes &mdash; subject, description, category, etc.</span></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        <strong>Important:</strong> Even when submitting anonymously, the feedback content itself
        (subject, description, category, type) is still stored in the database. Only the link between
        your account and that specific feedback record is removed. The system does not log your IP
        address alongside feedback submissions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. Session -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-session" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
        Session &amp; Technical Data
      </h2>
      <p>
        When you log in, the server creates a <strong>session</strong> that stores a minimal amount
        of information to keep you authenticated across page requests:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your internal <strong>user ID</strong> (a database integer).</li>
        <li>Your <strong>display name</strong>.</li>
        <li>Your <strong>role</strong> (<code>student</code> or <code>admin</code>).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Sessions are stored server-side and expire automatically after <strong>2 hours</strong> of
        inactivity. A session cookie is placed in your browser to identify your session. This cookie is:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Marked <code>HttpOnly</code> &mdash; it cannot be read by client-side JavaScript.</li>
        <li>Marked <code>SameSite=Lax</code> &mdash; it is not sent on cross-site requests.</li>
        <li>Marked <code>Secure</code> in production &mdash; it is only transmitted over HTTPS.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        The system uses <strong>Morgan</strong> for HTTP request logging. These server logs record
        the HTTP method, URL, status code, and response time for debugging purposes. They do not
        include the content of your submissions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 7. How we use -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-use" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">7</span>
        How We Use Your Information
      </h2>
      <p>
        Your information is used exclusively to operate the CSPC Suggestion &amp; Feedback System:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account management</strong> &mdash; to create, authenticate, and manage your account.</li>
        <li><strong>Feedback processing</strong> &mdash; to receive, categorize, track, and respond to your submissions.</li>
        <li><strong>Dashboard personalization</strong> &mdash; to display your own feedback and its current status on your personal dashboard (identified submissions only).</li>
        <li><strong>Administrator review</strong> &mdash; to allow authorized CSPC personnel to read, prioritize, update, and respond to feedback.</li>
        <li><strong>System security</strong> &mdash; to enforce rate limits, prevent abuse, and protect authenticated routes.</li>
        <li><strong>Aggregate statistics</strong> &mdash; the admin dashboard displays summary counts by status, category, and type. These statistics do not identify individual users.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not use your information for advertising, third-party analytics, or any purpose other
        than operating this feedback system.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 8. Who can access -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-access" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">8</span>
        Who Can Access Your Data
      </h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>You</strong> &mdash; you can view all of your own identified feedback submissions
          along with their full status history and admin responses on your personal dashboard.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authorized administrators</strong> &mdash; users with the <code>admin</code> role
          have access to all submitted feedback, including the submitter&rsquo;s name, email, and
          student ID for identified submissions. Administrators can update feedback status, add notes,
          and post responses. They cannot see who submitted anonymous feedback.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Other students</strong> &mdash; cannot access other students&rsquo; feedback. Every
          student query is scoped to their own user ID at the database query level.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Third parties</strong> &mdash; no personal data is shared with any third party,
          with the exception of Google&rsquo;s OAuth service during login (see Section 3a). No
          analytics or advertising services are integrated.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 9. Database storage -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-storage" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">9</span>
        Database Storage
      </h2>
      <p>
        All data is stored in a <strong>MySQL</strong> relational database. The database contains
        the following tables that hold personal or submission data:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>users</strong> &mdash; stores account information (name, email, password hash, Google ID, avatar URL, role, student ID, department).</li>
        <li><strong>feedback</strong> &mdash; stores all feedback submissions.</li>
        <li><strong>feedback_status_history</strong> &mdash; stores every status change for each feedback item.</li>
        <li><strong>feedback_responses</strong> &mdash; stores administrator responses to feedback items.</li>
        <li><strong>categories</strong> &mdash; stores the available feedback categories (no personal data).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All database queries use <strong>parameterized statements</strong> to prevent SQL injection.
        Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes; no plain-text password is retained anywhere in the system.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 10. Email -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-email" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">10</span>
        Email Communication
      </h2>
      <p>
        The current implementation of this system <strong>does not send any email notifications</strong>.
        Administrator responses are posted directly to the feedback detail page and are visible when
        you log in and view that submission. No automated emails are sent to users at any point.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 11. Retention -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-retention" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">11</span>
        Data Retention
      </h2>
      <p>
        The current system does not implement an automated data deletion or account deactivation
        workflow accessible to students. Specifically:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Accounts</strong> can be marked inactive by a database administrator. An inactive
          account cannot log in. There is no self-service account deletion feature in the current interface.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Feedback submissions</strong> remain in the database until manually removed by a
          database administrator. The application interface does not currently provide a
          &ldquo;delete feedback&rdquo; feature for students or admins.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>If a user account is deleted</strong> from the database directly, the schema sets
          the <code>user_id</code> field on that user&rsquo;s feedback records to <code>NULL</code>
          (via <code>ON DELETE SET NULL</code>), effectively de-linking the submissions from the
          deleted account while retaining the feedback content.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you would like your account or submitted data reviewed or removed, please contact us using
        the information in Section 13.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 12. Security -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-security" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">12</span>
        Security Measures
      </h2>
      <p>
        The following security measures are implemented in the current codebase:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Helmet.js security headers</strong> &mdash; sets HTTP security headers including <code>Content-Security-Policy</code> and <code>X-Frame-Options</code> on every response.</li>
        <li><strong>HTTPS enforcement</strong> &mdash; session cookies are marked <code>Secure</code> in the production environment, ensuring they are only transmitted over HTTPS.</li>
        <li><strong>HttpOnly cookies</strong> &mdash; session cookies cannot be read by browser JavaScript, mitigating XSS-related session theft.</li>
        <li><strong>bcrypt password hashing</strong> &mdash; passwords for manual accounts are stored as bcrypt hashes; plain-text passwords are never persisted.</li>
        <li><strong>Parameterized SQL queries</strong> &mdash; all database queries use parameterized statements; no string concatenation is used for SQL, preventing SQL injection.</li>
        <li><strong>Rate limiting</strong> &mdash; the login, registration, and feedback submission endpoints have per-IP rate limits to deter brute-force and spam attacks.</li>
        <li><strong>Ownership-scoped queries</strong> &mdash; student queries always include a <code>WHERE user_id = ?</code> condition enforced at the database level, preventing cross-account data access.</li>
        <li><strong>Role-based access control</strong> &mdash; roles are stored in the database and checked server-side on every protected route; they cannot be escalated through the client.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        As this is an academic project, it may not implement the full depth of security controls
        found in commercial production systems. No system can guarantee absolute security.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- 13. Contact -->
    <section class="policy-section">
      <span class="policy-section__anchor" id="section-contact" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <h2 class="policy-section__heading">
        <span class="policy-section__heading-num" aria-hidden="true">13</span>
        Contact &amp; Questions
      </h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, want to request access to your data, or
        would like to ask about account or data removal, please contact the system administrator:
      </p>
      <div class="contact-card" role="region" aria-label="Contact information">
        <span class="contact-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">🏫</span>
        <div class="contact-card__content">
          <p><strong>Institution:</strong> Camarines Sur Polytechnic Colleges (CSPC)</p>
          <p><strong>System:</strong> CSPC Suggestion &amp; Feedback System</p>
          <p>
            You may reach the system administrator by submitting an inquiry through the feedback
            system itself after logging in, or by contacting the relevant CSPC office directly.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:var(--space-3); font-size:0.8rem; color:var(--color-text-light);">
            This is an academic project system. It does not claim compliance with any specific data
            protection law or regulation. If you have a concern about your data, we will do our best
            to address it promptly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div><!-- /.privacy-body -->

